        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Several competing stablecoins (Halo HUSD, Startale USDSC, and others) all depend on the same small set of infrastructure providers like M0, concentrating systemic risk in otherwise-distinct-looking products.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Simultaneous and divergent rule-making across the EU (MiCA), US (GENIUS Act trajectory), Hong Kong, and Japan creates compliance fragmentation; products legal in one jurisdiction may be non-compliant in another without re-architecture.",
          "source": "https://thegraph.com/blog/stablecoin-compliance-infrastructure-regulatory-readiness/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Spark's analysis highlights that institutional vault design now prioritizes withdrawal certainty over yield, signaling that redemption-path guarantees — not APY — are the liquidity stress point issuers must engineer around.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market / collateral",
